{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788185266,"nonce":"/B7HawORPCVuHQfzB65VXAf1iLE=","message":"SEED LESSON from Evan, 2026-08-31 (session 7), caught live at the bench.\n\n**A queued medical bill does nothing unless some OTHER pawn has that work type\nCHECKED. A pawn cannot operate on themselves.**\n\nWhat happened: I queued `InstallBionicLeg` on Rubio, gave Valentin Medicine 20,\nand advanced expecting to watch Rubio walk to the hospital bed. Evan stopped it:\n\"noone is assigned doctor but rubio so he won't walk to the bed.\" He was right,\nand the observer confirmed it exactly — Doctor was 3 (checked) on Rubio, the\nPATIENT, and 0 on all three other colonists including the surgeon I had just\nskilled up. Nothing would ever have happened.\n\nThe lesson for the playbook, in the agent's terms:\n\n- With **manual priorities OFF** the Work tab is a checkbox column: priority `0`\n  means UNCHECKED, `3` means CHECKED. A colonist with maxed Medicine still will\n  not take a surgery job if their Doctor box is unchecked. Skill is not\n  assignment.\n- **The patient does not count.** Self-surgery is not a thing, so if the only\n  pawn with Doctor checked is the one on the table, the bill sits forever and\n  the patient never even walks to the bed — there is no job for anyone to take,\n  so nothing looks broken, it just silently never starts.\n- **The check to run after queuing any medical bill:** read the work column for\n  the whole roster and confirm at least one pawn OTHER than the patient has that\n  work type non-zero. `pawn {sections:[\"work\"]}` returns the full `row` with a\n  priority per work type; that is the read.\n- Same shape applies beyond medicine: a bill on any bench needs a pawn with the\n  relevant work checked who is not otherwise occupied. \"Nobody is assigned\" is a\n  silent failure mode, not an error.\n\nThis is the second time this session that the thing blocking a bill was CAPACITY\nrather than the verb: 3.4's bullet 4 also failed once because the colony had one\ndoctor and it was the patient. Worth a checklist line of its own — after any\nbill, ask who will actually do it.","files":null}]}